{"parentUuid":"27620080-b5c0-4282-91ce-1cdb48512f80","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgTzsb17nwfkD7qLTV2SQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YCxFKySqgbxgVD5z5j6rkP","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"r7-blocks","message":"Jarod picked Baseplate (option 2), with changes:\n1. LIGHT theme for Blocks: a paper/light ground instead of the cobalt field, and no big orange slabs (he doesn't like the persimmon name tile). Keep the tiles concept, the bricks nav and the socials-as-bricks, and the isometric JT assembly (which he loves). Cobalt and persimmon become accents on light. Re-colour the JT's faces so it reads on light: paper faces need a cobalt edge or a cobalt T, your call.\n2. Roles: the role line is changing site-wide to a <ul aria-label=\"Roles\"> of four items (Engineering Leader, Frontend Architecture, Design Engineering, Developer Experience) right after the h1, in label caps with square bullets. The info strip keeps only \"Open to new roles\". Copy that markup from prototypes/r7/roleline/options/2/ into your seed. In Baseplate the roles sit inside the name tile, under the name.\nMake 2 light palette variants of Baseplate (e.g. warm paper vs cool white; persimmon vs cobalt as the lead accent) at options/2a and 2b, same rules (same markup, override CSS only, AA contrast; note new knobs). Shots at 390 and 1440, and update index.html. Report ≤ 120 words.","type":"message","recipient":"r7-blocks","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Jarod picked Baseplate (option 2), with changes:\n1…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3303,"cache_read_input_tokens":279736,"output_tokens":2104,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":385},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input